## Digest §T17 (Packet #12, video-digests/2026-11-17-yt-ajavsmbcapy/digest.md)
- Timestamps: 4:31–5:05
- Mechanics: State tiles arranged in two labelled camps (South pro-slavery / North anti-slavery); arrows move population between categories as the narration explains that only free people were proposed to count, and the South wanted enslaved people counted (transcript 4:37–4:55).
- Why it works: The founding bargain is drawn with the same tile grammar as the modern data (T16) — the system's present and its origin share one visual language, so the continuity claim is visible, not just narrated.
- Evidence: ev/t282-north-south-tiles.jpg (North/South tile diagram, 282 s)

## Style-library techniques-diagrams.md §T218
- Tier: DESCRIBED — OWED #100
- Mechanics: state tiles arranged in two labelled camps (South pro-slavery / North anti-slavery); arrows move population between categories as the narration explains that only free people were proposed to count, and the South wanted enslaved people counted (transcript 4:37–4:55). Operation: tile move as re-categorisation. The founding bargain is drawn with the same tile grammar as the modern data (T217), so the continuity claim is visible, not just narrated.
- Feeds: diagram — P12 @ 4:31–5:05 — ev/t282-north-south-tiles.jpg

## Packet identity / gaps
Packet #12 (Vox "The Electoral College, explained", ajavsMbCapY, 488.301 s, source.webm 1920×1080 VP9). Packet adopted WITH GAPS; the digest's gap list does not name T17/T218 (the clip-filename offset gap attaches to clip-cited techniques; T218 has no clip). No prior attempt exists for T218: no scores.md, no codex/ returns, no verdict-history line (first attempt, queue #100). Family siblings in Packet #12: T210 grid-map PASS 85.2 (Wave 35) · T212 margin bar field NO VERDICT (Wave 35, completion charged to Wave 36).

## QUEUE.md recreation section (read this cycle)
Wave 35 update: "DESCRIBED-OWED 6 (rows #100–#105: T218 · T219 · T227 · T232 · T233 · T238)". T218 = row #100, OWED/DESCRIBED, first attempt owned by recreation (Amendment A3 §3).

