169:**Pacing curve:** monotonic narration deceleration (183 → 169 → 154/157 → 144 wpm) against roughly constant visual grammar — the film slows down as its claims get heavier. **Where it stalls:** S5's first half (6:30–7:10, T21) re-prices the S2 ratio point in present-day data at chart level before the 1948 callback re-earns momentum. **Length pricing (Amendment A3, >5 min):** the length BUYS the history section — the present-day claim (§5 G5) only lands because S4's dated sequence precedes it; the SAG is T21's restatement stretch (~40 s that repeat S2's conclusion in new charts); the COMPRESSION FLOOR is ≈5 min — keep S1's montage hook, S2's TX/VT pair + threshold, S3's margin field + California price, a compressed S4 (three-fifths scoreboard + 1969 block), and the coda quote; drop T05/T15's secondary charts and T21's demographic bars.
174:- **G1 — One substance, every job (0:28–8:08).** The dot grid is title (T03), tally (T09), and outro (T22); tiles serve modern data (T16) and founding history (T17). The viewer learns two representations in eight minutes and reads everything with them.
175:- **G2 — The margin is shown before it is erased (2:37–2:52).** T11 draws every state's losing share as dotted matter before T13 states the rule that discards it — the film's central unfairness is demonstrated, not asserted.
176:- **G3 — Sourced graphics at the surprising points (0:54, 3:59, 6:17).** The Gallup trend is named on its chart (T05); the influence grid credits Mixon, Duquette, Cebula 2017 on its face (T16); the Allen quote card prints "Source: Alexander Keyssar" (T20). The three least believable exhibits carry their provenance.
177:- **G4 — The worked pair is staged fairly before it is indicted (1:24–2:19).** TX/VT is shown near-proportional at the House stage (T07) before the +2 step creates the distortion (T08) — the film isolates the exact operation it criticises.
178:- **G5 — History is load-bearing, not decorative (4:21–6:30).** S4's dated sequence (three-fifths scoreboard T18 → reform timeline T19 → defenders' quotes T20) is what entitles the coda's generalisation at 7:46; cut S4 and the ending is an opinion.
179:- **G6 — Numbers arrive as verdicts (1:51, 2:51, 3:58).** The figures that matter (210,000 ringed; 1% → 100%; 51×) land after their diagrams are built, each as the last element of its scene — the numeral is the punchline of a constructed proof.
199:- **L7 — Same tiles, changed rules (worked-example reuse).** Container: **diagram**. Class: **storytelling pattern**. Consumer: DLC assembler. TX/VT recurs at three stages (T07→T08); North/South tiles carry two population definitions (T17) — hold the representation still and vary the rule, so the rule is what the viewer sees change (codex-observe P-A5(b), checked and standing). Build cost: **cheap** — state persistence in the scene graph.
